<section class="section section--flush-top" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2>Five ways the platform watches, reads, and supports.</h2>
      <p>Each AI capability runs on a different kind of input — sensor readings, written notes, permit text, or a photograph — and reports back in the same structured way.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="capability">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">01 — Anomaly detection</p>
        <h3 class="h4">24/7 monitoring across SCADA &amp; historian feeds</h3>
        <p>Every connected sensor and instrument feed is watched continuously against its own learned baseline — not a fixed threshold someone set once and forgot. A reading doesn't have to breach a hard limit to get flagged, just behave differently than it normally does.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/ai/anomaly-detection.webp" width="455" height="279" alt="Anomaly on compressor C-4, vibration tag VIB-0412 from a live SCADA feed: baseline 0.18 in/s, current reading 0.41 in/s, a 128% deviation from the 7-day baseline. Flagged automatically with no manual threshold set for this tag." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability capability--flip">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">02 — Sentiment analysis</p>
        <h3 class="h4">The tone behind inspections &amp; work orders</h3>
        <p>Written notes carry more than the checkbox does — a technician's language can signal urgency or frustration well before it's stated outright. Sentiment analysis flags that tone and prioritizes attention; it doesn't replace a person's judgment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/ai/sentiment-analysis.webp" width="455" height="266" alt="Sentiment on work order WO-8823 notes for Skid A-114: elevated, with urgency and frustration detected at 78, three severity levels above typical entries. Routed to a supervisor for review; a person still makes the call." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">03 — RAG</p>
        <h3 class="h4">Retrieval-augmented analysis of permit conditions</h3>
        <p>Permit documents run to dozens of pages of specific, binding conditions. Retrieval-augmented generation reads your actual permit text and answers against it directly — the citation comes from your document, not a generic answer about what permits usually say.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/ai/permit-query.webp" width="455" height="237" alt="Permit query on air permit TX-44921, condition 14(b): asked for the VOC limit for Skid A-114, answered 12.3 tons per year, cited from the permit document page 6, condition 14(b)." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability capability--flip">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">04 — AI assistant</p>
        <h3 class="h4">Ask it directly – regulatory &amp; environmental questions</h3>
        <p>The same retrieval layer sits behind a chat interface, so anyone on the team can ask a plain-language question about a regulation, a permit condition, an asset's current status, or your own data and get an answer sourced from your actual records.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/ai/ai-assistant.webp" width="455" height="291" alt="Assistant chat. Is Skid A-114 within its Title V limits? Yes, CO2 is at 72% of its permitted limit as of today, sourced from the Title V permit and emissions log. When's the next LDAR survey due? Oct 15, on a quarterly cycle per NSPS OOOOb, sourced from the requirement register." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">05 — Object recognition</p>
        <h3 class="h4">Reality capture for equipment identification</h3>
        <p>Point a camera at a piece of equipment and the model identifies its class and reads its markings — stencil ID, serial number, make and model — then reconciles that against the asset registry automatically, instead of a technician typing it in by hand.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/ai/reality-capture.webp" width="455" height="313" alt="Reality capture of pump P-08: a nameplate scan captured at 10:14 AM identifies a centrifugal pump, stencil ID P-08, serial number SN-88213X, and finds a matching make and model in the registry. Auto-matched to the existing asset record with no manual data entry." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

